LAMMPS (22 Jul 2025 - Update 4)
# Is alpha-Ga stable under this potential (2NN MEAM, Ga part of the Do-Shin-Lee 2009 Ga-In fit)?
# Run from metals/Ga/:  lmp -in stability/in.ga_stability.lmp -var T 302.92 -var seed 2026 -log stability/log.ga_stability
#   1. 0 K: relax alpha-Ga (Cmce, from data.solid.lmp) and fcc Ga, both with box relaxation -> E per atom
#   2. alpha-Ga NPT (aniso) at T for 20 ps: does it stay alpha-Ga? (displacements, box ratios, the 2.44 A dimer)
# Prints STABILITY lines that stability/check_ga.py turns into a pass/fail verdict.

variable        steps index 10000
variable        dt    index 0.002

units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p

# ---- 1a. alpha-Ga at 0 K
read_data       data.solid.lmp
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (22.595 22.977 22.63)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  600 atoms
  read_data CPU = 0.003 seconds
include         potential.mod
# Ga: 2NN MEAM, NIST IPR 2009--Do-E-C--Ga-In--LAMMPS--ipr1 (doi:10.1088/0953-8984/21/32/325801). Needs the MEAM package.
pair_style meam
pair_coeff * * potential/library.meam Ga In potential/GaIn.meam Ga
neighbor        1.0 bin
print           "STABILITY experimental_box $(lx:%.4f) $(ly:%.4f) $(lz:%.4f)"
STABILITY experimental_box 22.5950 22.9770 22.6300
thermo_style    custom step pe lx ly lz press
fix             br all box/relax aniso 0.0 vmax 0.001
minimize        1e-12 1e-12 20000 200000
Neighbor list info ...
  update: every = 1 steps, delay = 0 steps, check = yes
  max neighbors/atom: 2000, page size: 100000
  master list distance cutoff = 5
  ghost atom cutoff = 5
  binsize = 2.5, bins = 10 10 10
  2 neighbor lists, perpetual/occasional/extra = 2 0 0
  (1) pair meam, perpetual
      attributes: full, newton on
      pair build: full/bin/atomonly
      stencil: full/bin/3d
      bin: standard
  (2) pair meam, perpetual, half/full from (1)
      attributes: half, newton on
      pair build: halffull/newton
      stencil: none
      bin: none
